It calls the Glowmarkt API of Hildebrand Technology Limited
(https://api.glowmarkt.com/api/v0-1/), the cloud behind the Bright app, with
the e-mail and the password of the user's Bright account and the public
application id of the Bright app. Hildebrand, Glow, Glowmarkt and Bright are
trademarks of Hildebrand Technology Limited; this integration is not
affiliated with nor endorsed by Hildebrand.

Protocol knowledge
------------------
The endpoints, the parameters and the shapes of the answers come from the
official Swagger documents of the Glowmarkt API ("Resource System" and
"Virtual Entity System", https://api.glowmarkt.com/api-docs/v0-1/resourcesys/
and https://api.glowmarkt.com/api-docs/v0-1/vesys/, copyright Hildebrand
Technology Limited), read on 2026-10-28.

Facts were also read, without copying any code, in:
  - pyglowmarkt by cybermaggedon (https://github.com/cybermaggedon/pyglowmarkt,
    Apache License 2.0): the application id, the `currentRates` shape of the
    tariff, `nulls=1`, the `catchup` call;
  - the Home Assistant custom integration "Hildebrand Glow (DCC)" by Harley
    Watson (https://github.com/HandyHat/ha-hildebrandglow-dcc, MIT License):
    the classifiers, the costs in pence, the data about 30 minutes late;
  - glowmarkt-rs by David Townsend (https://github.com/Mossop/glowmarkt-rs,
    MIT License): the 10-day limit of a half-hourly reading, the `exp` of
    the sign-in answer.
This integration is an independent JavaScript implementation.
